task:
Performance review. The code or data is supplied inline. This is a diagnosis-only task: do NOT edit or create any file and do not run commands; respond with findings and a proposed fix as text. Be explicit about what you measured versus what you are inferring.

`yakos kanban --with-last-commit` renders a board with up to 300 items. Current implementation:

```go
func annotate(items []Item, repo string) {
	for i := range items {
		cmd := exec.Command("git", "-C", repo, "log", "-1", "--format=%h %s", "--", items[i].Path)
		out, err := cmd.Output()
		if err == nil {
			items[i].LastCommit = strings.TrimSpace(string(out))
		}
	}
}
```
Users report the command takes ~9 seconds on a large repo. Explain why, and propose the fix. Include at least two options with their tradeoffs and say which you would measure first.
